ans:
Export the frames as images of the same size first, then export the GIF. A working approach is:

bbox = MapThread[Max, Rasterize[#, "RasterSize"] & /@ list];
list2 = ImageCrop[Rasterize[#], bbox, Padding -> White] & /@ list;
Export["A://zod.gif", list2, "DisplayDurations" -> 3]

This makes every frame the same size before export, which avoids corruption. Then use the resulting GIF file in PowerPoint.

